<figure class="gateway-tls-paths" aria-labelledby="gateway-tls-title">
  <figcaption id="gateway-tls-title"><span class="content-kicker">Follow the encrypted segments</span><strong>“The Gateway uses TLS” does not say where plaintext exists.</strong></figcaption>
  <div class="tls-grid">
    <article>
      <header><b>HTTPS termination</b><small>HTTPRoute can match HTTP fields</small></header>
      <div><span>Client</span><i class="encrypted">TLS</i><span>Gateway<br/><em>decrypts</em></span><i>HTTP</i><span>Backend</span></div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <header><b>TLS passthrough</b><small>Routing uses pre-decryption information such as SNI</small></header>
      <div><span>Client</span><i class="encrypted">TLS</i><span>Gateway<br/><em>does not decrypt</em></span><i class="encrypted">TLS</i><span>Backend<br/><em>decrypts</em></span></div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <header><b>Terminate + backend TLS</b><small>Two separate TLS relationships and trust decisions</small></header>
      <div><span>Client</span><i class="encrypted">TLS 1</i><span>Gateway<br/><em>decrypts</em></span><i class="encrypted">TLS 2</i><span>Backend<br/><em>decrypts</em></span></div>
    </article>
  </div>
</figure>

